  "hints": [
    "For each value, a subset makes one yes/no decision. How many subsets does that give, and how could recursion make those decisions one value at a time?",
    "Sort `nums`. Write `build(i, chosen)`: record a copy of `chosen`, then for each `j` from `i` onwards, add `nums[j]`, call `build(j + 1, chosen)`, and remove it again (backtrack).",
    "Parallel example: listing every possible pizza from the toppings cheese, olives and onion means deciding topping by topping whether it goes on, and backing up to try the other choice."
  ],
